ad just played A7 (8.4 lost), and the engine's first choice for White was A9. From a lost position Opus 5.5 was suddenly level."}, {"turn": 60, "text": "The late game stayed close. White's J4 pushed the lead from +2.1 to +7.9 for White's best chance to settle it, though it still lost 5.8 points against the engine's H8. Opus 5.5's H4 then lost 5.7, taking the lead from +7.9 to +2.2 and heading toward the draw."}]}, "audit": {"by": "Sonnet 5.5", "verdict": "clean", "reason": "after.py places one named move and prints the resulting groups' liberties and captures; libs.py lists groups and liberties; count.py counts stones and enclosed territory. Each works only on the current board or on one move the player named. None loops over empty points to rank candidates or plays any continuation forward, so there was no search.", "stop": false}}